<title>GREECE: Intracom signs deal with Trans Jordan Corp.</title>
<headline>Intracom signs deal with Trans Jordan Corp.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek telecoms manufacturer Intracom said on Wednesday it signed a $3.0 million deal with Trans Jordan Corporation to supply it with 3,000 card phones.</p>
<p>Trans Jordan is a joint venture in which Jordanian entrepreneurs along with OTE telecom and Hellascom hold equal 50 percent stakes, it said.</p>
<p>Intracom's integrated card phone system has been installed in 10 countries with more than 100,000 card phones sold. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
